            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_2f249682">A4:005</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="fr">Pieces de conversation</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_6169e28c">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_20">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_21_0">
               <p xml:id="idm78">The collection consists of twelve character pieces for solo harpsichord, all in the same key. It is presumably one of the works listed in the Breitkopf auction catalogue of 1836 sold together with works by <persName xml:id="idm79" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Johann Heinrich Rolle</persName>; the collection is not found in any of the Breitkopf sales catalogues. It seems likely that the collection is an early work though the present transcription might indeed be of a much later date.</p>
            </history>
