            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_198ed7af">
               <titlePage label="" xml:id="titlePage_9eafe5ac">
                  <p xml:id="idm36">Pieces. | de Conversation | del Sig: Scheibe</p>
               </titlePage>
               <extent xml:id="extent_f713850d">3 bifolios</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_a8f56a26">35.1x21.9</dimensions>
               <watermark xml:id="watermark_9e482217">a faint emblem is visible; paper of a dense and good quality.</watermark>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_531040c2">In 2<rend xml:id="idm41" rend="sup">o</rend>; upright format, consisting of 3 nested bifolios, once sewn together; title page (fol. 1r), music (fols. 1v–6r), a different piece presumably not belonging to the collection (fol. 6v; SchW A4:004); in all 3 bifolios. Hand-ruled paper, 16 staves (9 mm; single rastrum used but in parts of two staves) in brown ink and music in black ink; two staves between two movements on fol. 2r, bottom two staves on fols. 3r–v, 4v and bottom four staves on fols. 4r, 5r have not been used. A clean copy. Title page: at top right-hand corner the shelf mark '1685' has been added in pencil, later cancelled in pencil; at top left-hand corner: '<rend xml:id="idm42" rend="line-through">21</rend> 18. <rend xml:id="idm43" rend="sup">2.b.</rend>' added in ink; at bottom left-hand corner a 'C' added in pencil. The source includes the following pieces: fols. 1v–2r: 'La Visite'; fol. 2r: 'Discours'; fol. 2v: 'Rejouissançe'; fols. 2v–3r: 'Compliment'; fol. 3r: 'Connoissance'; fol. 3v: 'Amour'; fol. 4r: 'Promenade'; fol. 4v: 'Jalousie'; fol. 5r: 'Ennuy'; fol. 5v: 'Querelle'; fols. 5v–6r: 'Dispute'; and fol. 6r: 'Reconciliation'.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
